<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Prestige & Willshaw (1975) & Brown et al. (2000) EphA/ephrin-A retinotectal chemoaffinity & synaptic competition — MorphoEval overall 56.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 baseline assessment of `1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py` (57.3/100). The baseline script evaluates a 1D pointwise argmin of the chemoaffinity energy E_chem(x,y) = 0.5*(R_A(x)*L_A(y) - gamma_0)^2 for wild-type and uncoupled knock-in shifts, but omits the 2D synaptic weight matrix ODE dW_ij/dt with Prestige-Willshaw Group II row/column synaptic competition and cooperative neighborhood coupling, cannot reproduce caudal displacement of wild-type Isl2- axons in Isl2-EphA3 ki/ki homozygotes or linear half-tectum compression / half-retina expansion, omits the Ephrin-A2/A5 double-knockout scrambled control, and displays the 72 hpf Danio rerio retinal confocal specimen without automated CV segmentation. Overall 56.3/100 (faithfulness 53.9, reproducibility 62.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 50, Parameter expressivity 55, Morphometric validation 54, Source and data traceability 66, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: docs/media/retinotectal_chemoaffinity_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 413209 B, 1320×1020 px, artifact_sha256 f19fc94ecfbc8595859748ac2db860d7be48578ec498607d7bd8f90ffcdccf60 (sha256 f19fc94ecfbc8595859748ac2db860d7be48578ec498607d7bd8f90ffcdccf60), spec_fingerprint 291d0b05f4ef97593e7998ed422cf0c6840ddc0d18ee83dd5143a46bbb22b878. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 291d0b05f4ef97593e7998ed422cf0c6840ddc0d18ee83dd5143a46bbb22b878; artifact_sha256: f19fc94ecfbc8595859748ac2db860d7be48578ec498607d7bd8f90ffcdccf60; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/paper_citations.bib=aad29a956cd55dc1..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/retinotectal_chemoaffinity_reference.json=86046fcab644c7a3..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/scout_manifest.json=5ccb8a42580e5070..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/zebrafish_retinotectal_specimen.jpg=e16ecb3325a48823...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add automated CV segmentation of the 72 hpf Danio rerio confocal retinal specimen (concentric inner/outer retinal lamina rings, radial fluorescence profile, and nasal-to-temporal RGC arc), and render a 9-panel dark-mode synthesis figure and 24-frame animated GIF.",
        "remediation needed: Implement the full 2D synaptic weight matrix ODE dW_ij/dt with Prestige-Willshaw Group II Sinkhorn-Knopp homeostatic row/column competition and cooperative retinal-tectal neighborhood coupling.",
        "remediation needed: Simulate all 6 canonical regimes: Wild-Type inverted map (slope -1.00), Brown et al. (2000) Isl2-EphA3/+ heterozygous and Isl2-EphA3/EphA3 homozygous duplicated maps, Prestige & Willshaw (1975) Group II half-tectum compression (slope -0.50) and half-retina expansion (slope -2.00), and Ephrin-A2/A5 DKO scrambled control." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.63e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
